I agree that people generally don't go around thinking A <=> ~A.  But
for many people, telling them that A <=> B, B <=> C, C <=> D, D <=> E,
and E <=> ~A will get nowhere--except that they will resent you for
being "smart" or even "stuck-up."  Most people won't sit still for a
five-minute proof that two of their ideas contradict each other (or
one contradicts itself)--much less exert the effort to generate the
proof themselves.  Even if they could.  And in some cases people are
taught to distrust logic, so that even though they would reject an
obvious contradiction, they would also reject any input that looked
like a proof, before they ever had a chance to apply it to their
beliefs.  You may belittle such people...

