Subject: [#94-3-244] Steganography and Copyright on the printed page

I found a paper called "Electronic Marking and Identification
Techniques to Discourasge Document Copying" available via anonymous
FTP from research.att.com, file "dist/brassil/infocom94.ps".  It
describes several techniques for invisibly encoding information in
electronically transmissable pages of text, and the results of
experiments where (with one of the techniques) the information was
reliably recovered from 10th generation photocopies of a printed
version of the text.

The information he has in mind uniquely identifies the legitimate
holder of a copyrighted document so illegal copying can be traced.

